00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.779
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.951
Grammar focus: Present perfect (I have improved).

55
00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:05.578
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:06.283 --> 00:03:07.888
I have improved my speaking.

57
00:03:08.783 --> 00:03:10.446
My confidence has grown.

58
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:13.408
We have learned two hundred words.

59
00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:17.400
Use the present perfect to talk about progress up to now.

60
00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:21.603
Be careful! Don't say: I have improve my speaking.

61
00:03:23.567 --> 00:03:25.961
Say: I have improved my speaking.

62
00:03:26.261 --> 00:03:28.713
After 'have', use the past participle.

63
00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:32.373
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:33.167 --> 00:03:34.226
